WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.970
-President Trump vowed
to do everything in his power

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.471
to fight the opioid epidemic

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:08.341
which takes the lives
of 174 people each day

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.777
ravaging communities
and ripping families apart.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.045
So what has Trump actually done
to tackle this issue,

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:14.113
and who's he putting in charge

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:15.648
of this enormously
important task?

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.450
It's time for "The Check In."

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.285
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.886
[ Bell dings ]

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:24.023
-America has about
4% of the world's population

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:27.393
but about 27% of the world's
drug overdose deaths.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:30.129
For now, opioid addiction
is one of those uniquely

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.865
American problems
like type 2 diabetes

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:35.435
and adults wearing shirts
with Disney characters on them.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:36.469
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.904
"Honey, we're going to
a fancy dinner."

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.939
"That's why I'm wearing
my Scrooge McDuck."

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.374
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:44.010
Though among other promises
to fight the opioid epidemic,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.379
Trump said he would increase
funding to give resources

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.147
to states that needed it most
right away.

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:49.715
So how did that go?

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:52.284
-Is the federal government
doing all it can to combat

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.019
America's opioid epidemic?

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:55.221
A former commissioner

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.989
of the Food and Drug
Administration says no.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:59.726
-We have heard a lot of talk
from the administration on this,

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.727
but we've yet to see
the President take the kind

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:05.631
of serious action that
this emergency demands.

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:07.433
-It just is a pitiful,

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.836
pitiful story when
it comes to the amount

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.772
of real federal effort
and leadership

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.607
on the part of the President.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:17.143
-Wow! And he's saying that
on Fox News.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.845
That's what Trump watches
to feel good about himself.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:22.181
That's like if the kid
tuned into "Mr. Rogers"

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.250
and Mr. Rogers said,
"News flash, snot nose.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.518
I don't want to be
your neighbor.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.787
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.756
How about that?"

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.193
So the man speaking so bluntly
about Trump's inaction

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:35.294
is former Democratic lawmaker
Patrick Kennedy,

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:38.531
who also happens to be
on Trump's opioid commission

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.833
and has called it a sham
and charade saying,

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.935
"This and the administration's
other efforts to address

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:45.305
the epidemic are tantamount
to reshuffling chairs

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.438
on the Titanic."

00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:48.107
But, of course,
this isn't the Titanic.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:49.442
If it were, Trump would have

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.278
already tried to Billy Zane
his way on to a lifeboat.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:55.114
-I have a child!
I have a child!

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:58.517
-Clear a path here!
-Please, I have a child.

00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:01.254
-[ As Trump ]
"His name is Eric."

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.388
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.357
[ As Eric ]
"Father, I'm 34!"

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.725
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.694
Now, one of the few concrete
plans Trump did announce

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:10.597
to confront this issue was
that the federal government

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.731
would start a massive
advertising campaign

00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:14.667
to get people,
especially children,

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.103
not to want to take drugs
in the first place.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.405
Ugh, we already tried this,
and it didn't work.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.441
But of course that's not
stopping Trump from trying.

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:26.346
-There is nothing desirable
about drugs.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.714
They're bad.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:30.282
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:33.887
-The problem -- the problem, of
course, is that there is

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.954
something desirable about drugs.

00:02:35.954 --> 00:02:37.857
They make you feel great.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.493
That's why we have a huge
problem with drug addiction

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:43.262
and no problem at all
with celery addiction.

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:44.630
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:47.433
You never hear anyone say,
"Yo, man, you got a stalk?"

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.268
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:51.871
And for years, doctors and
pharmaceutical companies

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.940
pushed opioids for everything
from root canals

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.808
to a twisted ankle,
and everybody said, "Cool,"

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.077
because the drugs
made them feel great.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.645
So we'll ask you again,
Mr. President,

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:01.013
how do you prevent addiction?

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:03.482
-Maybe by talking to youth

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:05.852
and telling them no good,

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:08.954
really bad for you in every way.

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:12.859
-Do you think anti-drug ads
work on Americans?

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.061
These are the same people
who saw a commercial

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:18.564
for Tide Pods and thought,
"I want to eat that."

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:23.235
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:26.706
I'll put it in my mouth.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.809
But I'm sure to lead
this important effort,

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:31.610
Trump chose someone
with experience

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.379
and impeccable credentials
in the field.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.948
So let me just take
a big sip of water

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:37.817
and find out who it is.

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.586
-Kellyanne Conway will lead
the White House's effort

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:43.122
to combat the opioid problem
across the country.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.693
-Were you expecting
a split take?

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.530
Because that part of me --
that part of me died months ago.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.397
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.397 --> 00:03:54.700
Reports say Kellyanne
isn't even heeding the advice

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:55.868
of actual policy experts

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.470
of those most affected
by the this tragedy.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.339
Now, before Kellyanne and Trump,

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.374
tackling this issue
had largely been the role

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.943
of the Office of National
Drug Control Policy.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.645
Under the previous
administration,

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:08.514
the small office was made up
of public health experts

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.983
and law enforcement
who had first-hand experience

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:12.151
dealing with this issue,

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.320
and here's what it's been like
under Trump.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.656
-The Office of National
Drug Control Policy,

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.958
the entity charged
with coordinating

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.194
the federal government's
counter-drug response

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.929
still does not have
a permanent director.

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:26.232
-The President is expected
to slash the budget

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:29.101
out of the Office of National
Drug Control Policy.

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:31.604
-Guess what --
This administration,

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.039
which talks a big game
about opioids

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:36.376
just proposed cutting

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:40.513
the agency's budget by 95%.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.715
-That's right. Last year,
the White House allocated

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:45.351
about $368 million
for the office,

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.519
and for next year's budget,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.821
they're only asking for
about $17 million.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.156
The office trying to stop
the opioid epidemic

00:04:51.156 --> 00:04:53.158
is getting less than
Mark Wahlberg got

00:04:53.158 --> 00:04:54.526
for "Daddy's Home 2."

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:56.628
[ Laughter ]
And just hearing that news,

00:04:56.628 --> 00:04:59.265
six more people
started taking opioids.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.466
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.201
But perhaps we should have
seen this coming.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:06.138
The former Deputy Chief of Staff
at ONDCP was Taylor Weyeneth

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:08.207
who was only 24 years old.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.976
But it's not just him.
According to Politico,

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:12.044
among the people working
on the public education campaign

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:13.779
that Trump promised
is Andrew Giuliani,

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:16.015
Rudy Giuliani's 32-year-old son

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.483
who's a White House
public liaison

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.318
and has no background
in drug policy.

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:21.454
Well, at least he's 32.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:22.655
Which, if you're doing the math,

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:25.491
means Giuliani had him
when he was 105.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.427
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:30.596
Now Trump's budget proposals
did ask for additional funding

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.897
to fight the opioid epidemic,

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:33.398
and the Justice Department
recently announced

00:05:33.398 --> 00:05:36.134
that it would go after opioid
manufacturers and distributors.

00:05:36.134 --> 00:05:37.636
Those are positive steps.

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:39.805
But at the same time, Trump
is trying also trying to repeal

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:42.074
the Affordable Care Act
and slash Medicaid programs

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:43.943
that already help people
who are addicted.

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:46.578
And that is, um -- What's
the phrase I'm looking for?

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:48.080
-No good. Really bad.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.682
-This has been "The Check In."

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.784
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.086
[ Bell dings ]

